From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SenkOS
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 18:34:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] backlight: pwm_bl: start the LED at a tenth when lit from off

The RG35XX SP's LED driver stays dark when it is started below about 5%,
but keeps running down to 1% once lit. Coming back from suspend or a
blank at a low level left the panel dark. Lit from off below a tenth of
the maximum, run at a tenth for 50 ms first, then at the level asked for.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/video/backlight/pwm_bl.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/video/backlight/pwm_bl.c b/drivers/video/backlight/pwm_bl.c
index d15bd6254..d47c0a80b 100644
--- a/drivers/video/backlight/pwm_bl.c
+++ b/drivers/video/backlight/pwm_bl.c
@@ -99,8 +99,18 @@ static int pwm_backlight_update_status(struct backlight_device *bl)
 
 	if (brightness > 0) {
 		pwm_get_state(pb->pwm, &state);
-		state.duty_cycle = compute_duty_cycle(pb, brightness, &state);
 		state.enabled = true;
+		/*
+		 * Some LED drivers stay dark when started at a low level, and
+		 * keep running at it once lit: from off, start at a tenth first.
+		 */
+		if (!pb->enabled && brightness < bl->props.max_brightness / 10) {
+			state.duty_cycle = compute_duty_cycle(pb, bl->props.max_brightness / 10, &state);
+			pwm_apply_might_sleep(pb->pwm, &state);
+			pwm_backlight_power_on(pb);
+			msleep(50);
+		}
+		state.duty_cycle = compute_duty_cycle(pb, brightness, &state);
 		pwm_apply_might_sleep(pb->pwm, &state);
 
 		pwm_backlight_power_on(pb);
